        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): preserve empty env var values in config resolution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nFixes two related issues where `resolveConfigValue` / `resolveConfigValueUncached` use `||` (boolean OR) instead of `??` (nullish coalescing), causing an explicitly-set empty environment variable to fall through to the literal config key name.\n\n**Bug 1 — resolver fallback semantics**: When `MY_API_KEY=\"\"`, the `||` operator treats empty string as falsy and returns the literal `\"MY_API_KEY\"` as the API credential. This produces a confusing \"invalid API key\" error from the provider instead of a clear \"not configured\" failure.\n\n**Bug 2 — auth status disagreement**: `ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus` uses a plain truthiness check (`if (process.env[key])`) that treats empty env vars the same as absent env vars. After the `??` fix, the runtime resolver returns `\"\"` (treated as missing auth), but the status path still reports `configured: true, source: \"models_json_key\"`. A custom provider can appear configured in status while runs fail as missing auth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n- Replaced `||` with `??` in both `resolveConfigValue` and `resolveConfigValueUncached` so that an explicitly-set empty environment variable is preserved rather than silently reinterpreted as a literal config string.\n- Updated `getProviderAuthStatus` to use `in` operator to distinguish \"env var set to empty\" from \"env var not set\", and return `configured: false` when the env var is explicitly empty — aligning status with the runtime resolver.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers who accidentally leave an API key env var set to empty will now get a clear \"API key not configured\" error (both at runtime and in status checks) instead of a confusing \"invalid API key\" error from their provider.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Negative control (pre-fix)\n```\nBUG: empty env returns key name \"EMPTY_KEY\" instead of \"\"\n  resolveConfigValue => \"EMPTY_KEY\" ← BUG!\n  resolveConfigValueUncached => \"EMPTY_KEY\" ← BUG!\n```\n\n### vitest (10 tests, all pass)\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\n### getProviderAuthStatus alignment\n| Scenario | Old status | New status | Runtime (after `??` fix) |\n|----------|-----------|-----------|--------------------------|\n| Env var = `\"sk-real\"` | `configured: true, env` | `configured: true, env` ✅ | auth succeeds |\n| Env var = `\"\"` | `configured: true, models_json_key` ❌ | `configured: false` ✅ | auth missing |\n| Env var absent | `configured: true, models_json_key` | `configured: true, models_json_key` ✅ | literal fallback |\n| Shell command `!echo` | `configured: true, models_json_command` | `configured: true, models_json_command` ✅ | command fallback |\n\n### Files changed\n- `src/agents/sessions/resolve-config-value.ts`: `||` → `??` (2 chars × 2 sites)\n- `src/agents/sessions/model-registry.ts`: `getProviderAuthStatus` empty-env handling\n- `src/agents/sessions/resolve-config-value.test.ts`: +87 lines, 10 test cases",
        "branch": "fix/config-value-empty-env-fallback",
